#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:89
#: 06a61e4e917f4deaab954216cb51b0d4
msgid "Getting to the boot screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:92
#: 0b6a9150b4a2455e98f49aad4bdb96bb
msgid ""
"“Booting” is the process of starting your computer. When a computer boots "
"up, it first runs :term:`low-level software <firmware>` before the main "
"operating system. Depending on the computer, this low-level software may be "
"called the `“BIOS” <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BIOS>`__ or `“UEFI” "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unified_Extensible_Firmware_Interface>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:94
#: 3379bd1d37234c9b9838c1d5eb9d9319
msgid ""
"Since you’re installing Qubes OS, you’ll need to access your computer’s BIOS "
"or UEFI menu so that you can tell it to boot from the USB drive to which you "
"just copied the Qubes installer ISO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:96
#: 206a6db38e3d49f3aa48d0dafecacb6e
msgid ""
"To begin, power off your computer and plug the USB drive into a USB port, "
"but don’t press the power button yet. Right after you press the power "
"button, you’ll have to immediately press a specific key to enter the BIOS or "
"UEFI menu. The key to press varies from brand to "
"brand. :kbd:`Esc`, :kbd:`Del`, and :kbd:`F10` are common ones. If you’re not "
"sure, you can search the web for ``<COMPUTER_MODEL> BIOS key`` or "
"``<COMPUTER_MODEL> UEFI key`` (replacing ``<COMPUTER_MODEL>`` with your "
"specific computer model) or look it up in your computer’s manual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:98
#: 1a53042003f34af2a30d61c281997e1b
msgid ""
"Once you know the key to press, press your computer’s power button, then "
"repeatedly press that key until you’ve entered your computer’s BIOS or UEFI "
"menu. To give you an idea of what you should be looking for, we’ve provided "
"a couple of example photos below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:100
#: d89b1feea97042bc81f7b2c7fa14f1b7
msgid "Here’s an example of what the BIOS menu looks like on a ThinkPad T430:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:102
#: 40ae37d1edde4d18a1dc6c95d4dfd7b9
msgid "|ThinkPad T430 BIOS menu|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:378
#: ece0371c2f02424488ffea5add596cc9
msgid "ThinkPad T430 BIOS menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:104
#: 5be2423954714cc2add366e04b390b67
msgid "And here’s an example of what a modern UEFI menu looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:106
#: f398173f36d0483598f3c9c1ce8e7655
msgid "|UEFI menu|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:379
#: 1d8f3f73045044499899e71a74b21db3
msgid "UEFI menu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:108
#: 5778c7c9fcda49038416988397d8b29d
msgid ""
"Once you access your computer’s BIOS or UEFI menu, you’ll want to go to the "
"“boot menu”, which is where you tell your computer which devices to boot "
"from. The goal is to tell the computer to boot from your USB drive so that "
"you can run the Qubes installer. If your boot menu lets you select which "
"device to boot from first, simply select your USB drive. (If you have "
"multiple entries that all look similar to your USB drive, and you’re not "
"sure which one is correct, one option is just to try each one until it "
"works.) If, on the other hand, your boot menu presents you with a list of "
"boot devices in order, then you’ll want to move your USB drive to the top so "
"that the Qubes installer runs before anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:110
#: cc786413da454ec2a07b87332af24d70
msgid ""
"Then, if you are on a computer using UEFI, you’ll have to disable `Secure "
"Boot <https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/UEFI#SECURE-BOOT>`__ to allow Qubes OS "
"to boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:112
#: f0a90c71d9014aeebd8b47fc2809e6eb
msgid ""
"Once you’re done with the settings, save your changes. How you do this "
"depends on your BIOS or UEFI, but the instructions should be displayed right "
"there on the screen or in a nearby tab. (If you’re not sure whether you’ve "
"saved your changes correctly, you can always reboot your computer and go "
"back into the boot menu to check whether it still reflects your changes.) "
"Once your BIOS or UEFI is configured the way you want it, reboot your "
"computer. This time, don’t press any special keys. Instead, let the BIOS or "
"UEFI load and let your computer boot from your USB drive. If you’re "
"successful in this step, after a few seconds you’ll be presented with the "
"Qubes installer screen:"
msgstr ""

