#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:268
#: 75f577d34d1b497ba32b8ced132753cc
msgid ""
"By default, the installer will create a number of :term:`qubes <qube>` "
"(depending on the options you selected during the installation process). "
"These are designed to give you a more ready-to-use environment from the get-"
"go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:270
#: 11ab85a2c75741b6a193e8b2c287dbbc
msgid "Let’s briefly go over the options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:273
#: db2a4029bf7548b0973192dd6d5041d8
msgid "Templates Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:275
#: 132f9dff91ce4f1bbc2bbdd269440a54
msgid ""
"This section provides the :term:`templates <template>` you wish to install "
"and which one to use as the default one. The default template settings can "
"always be changed after this initial configuration too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:278
#: 257289e24bdd4b96ae54da100bec3b40
msgid "Main Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:280
#: 053b7346786643d68439c4f22a5bea3e
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Create default system qubes (sys-net, sys-firewall, default "
"DispVM)`: These are the core components of the system, required for things "
"like internet access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:282
#: f2977186bb3b456fbdbc8b2232b317db
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Make sys-firewall and sys-usb disposable`: The :term:`qubes "
"<qube>` responsible for firewalling/isolating network traffic and holding "
"certain hardware devices like USB, Bluetooth adapter, integrated cameras, "
"etc. (**sys-usb** only, if applicable) will be made :term:`disposable`. "
"Enabled by default as it fits most users' needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:284
#: d7472c6cd209454f9ef7fbde950caed0
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Make sys-net disposable`: The :term:`net qube` handling your "
"network devices will be made :term:`disposable`. This will result in loss of "
"stored Wi-Fi passwords and therefore automatic Wi-Fi connections each "
"time :term:`the qube <net qube>` gets booted. Disabled by default for a more "
"user-friendly experience but if you don't mind storing the aforementioned "
"passwords e.g. in an offline password manager, you may turn it on for "
"privacy enhancements (no broadcasting of saved Wi-Fi network names). You "
"might also :ref:`customize the disposable net qube so that your Wi-Fi "
"credentials will be passed dynamically <user/advanced-topics/disposable-"
"customization:Change application settings dynamically>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:286
#: 5b4feb1a5ab74edf9fad52ce367dffc8
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Preload disposable qubes based on the default DispVM (faster "
"usage)`: If your computer has enough memory, this option will be enabled by "
"default and :ref:`transparently enqueue several disposables in the "
"background for faster startup <user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-"
"disposables:Faster disposable startup (preloading)>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:288
#: ad25bc773cb446e485b08921f834b74d
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Create default application qubes (personal, work, untrusted, "
"vault)`: These are how you compartmentalize your digital life. There's "
"nothing special about the ones the installer creates. They're just "
"suggestions that apply to most people. If you decide you don't want them, "
"you can always delete them later, and you can always :doc:`create your own </"
"user/how-to-guides/how-to-organize-your-qubes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:290
#: 17755b3691f4442d9f7e5b28ee75f95a
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Use a qube to hold all USB controllers (create a new qube called "
"sys-usb by default)`: A dedicated :term:`qube` that holds certain hardware "
"devices like USB, Bluetooth adapter, integrated cameras, etc. (**sys-usb**) "
"will be created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:292
#: f250184a06204be4b926993d5614014a
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Use sys-net qube for both networking and USB devices`: certain "
"hardware devices will be held by **sys-net** instead. You should select this "
"option if you rely on a USB device for network access, such as a USB modem "
"or a USB Wi-Fi adapter, as this option will make the experience with them "
"more user-friendly and seamless."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:294
#: b1770b78329648adb37d86ee5e72195c
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Automatically accept USB mice (discouraged)`: If enabled, upon "
"the connecting of a device that presents itself as a USB mouse, it will be "
"automatically forwarded to :term:`dom0`. Disabled by default so once such "
"device is connected, manual user interaction is required to confirm "
"forwarding that device. This results in additional security benefits - e.g. "
"a malicious device presenting itself as a mouse will be rendered useless "
"until a confirmation dialog in :term:`dom0` is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:296
#: b939b64fd93043c4851a8fbe3cdf7c4b
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Automatically accept USB keyboard (discouraged if non-USB "
"keyboard is available)`: See the point above about USB mice. The same "
"applies here. Enabling this is mostly beneficial to modern stationary "
"workstations where only a USB keyboard can be used for typing. If you can "
"use a PS/2 keyboard (generally laptops use an emulated PS/2 for their "
"internal keyboards), you may want to leave this option disabled for "
"additional security."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:300
#: 7ba610ee08bd424abae195315886ef0f
msgid ""
"**Note:** When choosing to automatically accept USB mice or keyboards, be "
"aware of the :ref:`security considerations <user/security-in-qubes/device-"
"handling-security:USB Security>`. For troubleshooting non-working devices, "
"see :ref:`this document <user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-usb-devices:Using USB "
"keyboards and other input devices>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:302
#: 256af2d0139942d2863d0e277cfab18c
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Create Whonix Gateway and Workstation qubes (sys-whonix, anon-"
"whonix)`: If you want to use `Whonix <https://www.whonix.org/wiki/Qubes>`__, "
"you should select this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:304
#: 0ffe814e9b2f4c23a64e75b917c1f0a1
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Enable system and template updates over the Tor anonymity network "
"using Whonix`: If you select this option, then whenever you install or "
"update software in :term:`dom0` or a :term:`templates <template>`, the "
"internet traffic will go through Tor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:307
#: 65dedcf678f548a1b68b852a76329bbb
msgid "Advanced Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:309
#: e6a37839851245959aa36f16df43cfc4
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Use custom storage pool`: Here you can specify custom names for "
"the LVM pool holding your :term:`qubes <qube>`' filesystems as well as LVM "
"Volume Group name. Unless you're preparing a customized environment on your "
"machine (e.g. dual booting distinct Qubes OS releases), you can leave this "
"option unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:311
#: 80ab1d36995b404da08fabf99570adb1
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Do not configure anything (for advanced users)`: This is for very "
"advanced users only. If you select this option, you'll have to set "
"everything up manually afterward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide.rst:314
#: 66ddc997079b4645aae16c3f64aeb530
msgid ""
"When you’re satisfied with your choices, press **Done**. This configuration "
"process may take a while, depending on the speed of your computer and the "
"selected options described above (the more :term:`templates <template>` to "
"be installed, the longer the configuration process will take)."
msgstr ""

